<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  launchd job for the x lane, in the USER domain (a LaunchAgent).

  WHY AN AGENT, NOT THE DAEMON. Two separate reasons, either one sufficient.
  ego lite is a GUI app and will not start without an Aqua session, the same wall
  the ask lane hits. And `xw` runs the Claude CLI, whose credential is an OAuth
  login sitting in the login keychain -- which a system-domain process cannot
  unlock. The daemon would fail both halves of this job, silently, at 3am.

  AND A THIRD REASON THIS LANE HAS ALONE. grok.com puts an age-confirmation modal
  in the way, once per ego lite task space, and x-recon will not click it -- an age
  attestation is a statement about a person, not a checkbox a job may tick. That
  gate is cleared by a human at this machine or not at all, so there is no version
  of this lane that runs somewhere nobody is sitting.

  THE PRICE. An agent starts at login, not at boot, so this needs Automatic login
  on and FileVault off, exactly as com.eternalgy.gmapworker.ask.plist explains.

  PATH carries __HOME__/.local/bin because `claude` and `ego-browser` are both
  installed there, and /usr/bin because `xw` uses `jq`. A launchd job inherits
  no PATH worth having.

  Install it with the sed line in README.md -- launchd does not expand ~, so
  __HOME__ and __NODE__ must be real paths before this file is loaded.

  WORKER_TYPES pins this process to the x lane alone. One Grok ask is 40-120s and
  a lead may spend four of them, so it must not share a lane with the wrapper
  types that answer in seconds. It drives a different ego lite task space from the
  fb lane, so the two do not contend for a browser.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.eternalgy.gmapworker.x</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__NODE__</string>
    <string>__HOME__/automation-tools/worker/macmini.mjs</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>__HOME__/automation-tools</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/gmap-worker-x.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/gmap-worker-x.log</string>

  <!--
    No LAB_TOKEN here. macmini.mjs reads it from ~/.gmap-worker.env at chmod 600,
    for the same reason every other lane does: a plist is readable by every
    process on the box.
  -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>__HOME__</string>
    <key>WORKER_NAME</key>
    <string>macmini-x</string>
    <key>WORKER_TYPES</key>
    <string>x.subject,x.company,x.probe</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
